10 REM PRINT.BASIC: "?" is PRINT's short form -- the same statement under
20 REM a shorter name, not a related one, which is why the manual says
30 REM LIST writes it back out as PRINT. Everything PRINT accepts it
40 REM accepts: separators, print zones, a trailing semicolon, and USING.
50 ? "one"
60 ? "a","b"
70 ? "x";
80 ? "y"
90 ? USING "##.##"; 3.14159
100 ? 
110 ? &H10
120 END
